---
// ===========================================================================
// WriteFlow.astro — one keystroke, drawn.
//
// It replaces four paragraphs that said the same thing in order, because the
// thing being described IS an order: what is written, when the pass happens,
// and why the pass being big does not make the notification big.
//
// Inline SVG with the MD3 tokens as fills, so it themes with the page and
// carries no request of its own. The viewBox scales it; the text is kept
// large enough to survive that.
// ===========================================================================
---

<figure class="mt-8">
  <!-- Scrolls rather than shrinks. Scaled to a 375px column the labels come
       out around five pixels tall, which is a diagram nobody can read; the
       minimum width keeps them legible and the page still never scrolls. -->
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 720 392"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="writeflow-title writeflow-desc"
    class="w-full min-w-[620px]"
  >
    <title id="writeflow-title">What one keystroke does</title>
    <desc id="writeflow-desc">
      setValue writes the root, the leaf and its dirty flag, plus any container
      someone is reading. The validation request is coalesced into one
      microtask, which judges the whole root once. The verdict is diffed per
      path, so only the cells whose issues actually changed notify, and React
      commits only those components.
    </desc>

    <defs>
      <marker
        id="writeflow-arrow"
        viewBox="0 0 10 10"
        refX="9"
        refY="5"
        markerWidth="6"
        markerHeight="6"
        orient="auto-start-reverse"
      >
        <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="var(--md-outline)" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <g
      font-family="var(--md-font-sans, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif)"
      fill="var(--md-on-surface)"
    >
      <!-- 1. the write -->
      <rect x="16" y="8" width="330" height="44" rx="8"
        fill="var(--md-primary-container)" />
      <text x="32" y="30" font-size="14" font-weight="600"
        fill="var(--md-on-primary-container)">setValue("billing.postcode", "999")</text>
      <text x="32" y="45" font-size="11.5"
        fill="var(--md-on-primary-container)">synchronous, inside your event handler</text>

      <line x1="60" y1="52" x2="60" y2="76" stroke="var(--md-outline)"
        stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#writeflow-arrow)" />

      <!-- 2. fan-out -->
      <rect x="16" y="80" width="330" height="76" rx="8"
        fill="var(--md-surface-container-high)" stroke="var(--md-outline-variant)" />
      <text x="32" y="102" font-size="13" font-weight="600">fan-out — 3 cells</text>
      <text x="32" y="121" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--md-on-surface-variant)">the root · that leaf · its dirty flag</text>
      <text x="32" y="139" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--md-on-surface-variant)">containers only if somebody is reading one</text>
      <text x="368" y="121" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--md-on-surface-variant)">Whatever the depth of the path.</text>
      <text x="368" y="139" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--md-on-surface-variant)">A leaf edit is not a tree walk.</text>

      <line x1="60" y1="156" x2="60" y2="180" stroke="var(--md-outline)"
        stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#writeflow-arrow)" />

      <!-- 3. coalesce -->
      <rect x="16" y="184" width="330" height="60" rx="8"
        fill="var(--md-surface-container-high)" stroke="var(--md-outline-variant)" />
      <text x="32" y="206" font-size="13" font-weight="600">one microtask</text>
      <text x="32" y="226" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--md-on-surface-variant)">every write of this turn, coalesced into one request</text>
      <text x="368" y="206" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--md-on-surface-variant)">After the handler returns,</text>
      <text x="368" y="224" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--md-on-surface-variant)">before the browser paints.</text>
      <text x="368" y="242" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--md-on-surface-variant)">Three writes → one pass.</text>

      <line x1="60" y1="244" x2="60" y2="268" stroke="var(--md-outline)"
        stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#writeflow-arrow)" />

      <!-- 4. the pass -->
      <rect x="16" y="272" width="330" height="44" rx="8"
        fill="var(--md-secondary-container)" />
      <text x="32" y="294" font-size="13" font-weight="600"
        fill="var(--md-on-secondary-container)">validate(root) — the whole root, once</text>
      <text x="32" y="309" font-size="11.5"
        fill="var(--md-on-secondary-container)">which is how a rule can report against another field</text>

      <line x1="60" y1="316" x2="60" y2="340" stroke="var(--md-outline)"
        stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#writeflow-arrow)" />

      <!-- 5. the diff -->
      <rect x="16" y="344" width="330" height="44" rx="8"
        fill="var(--md-surface-container-high)" stroke="var(--md-outline-variant)" />
      <text x="32" y="366" font-size="13" font-weight="600">issue diff — writes only what moved</text>
      <text x="32" y="381" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--md-on-surface-variant)">400 fields judged; the one whose error changed wakes</text>
      <text x="368" y="366" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--md-on-surface-variant)">Compute is the schema's size.</text>
      <text x="368" y="384" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--md-on-surface-variant)">Notification is what changed.</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
    The last box is the one that matters: the pass is proportional to the
    schema, and the <em>notification</em> is proportional to what actually
    moved. The demo above is this diagram running — one pass per settled
    change, and a render count that only moves on the rows whose cells did.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
